### ============================================
### Course Manager — API Test File
### Use with IntelliJ HTTP Client (click green play buttons)
### ============================================

### ==================== DEPARTMENTS ====================

### Get all departments
GET http://localhost:8080/api/departments
Accept: application/json

###

### Get department by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/departments/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Get department that doesn't exist (should return 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/departments/999
Accept: application/json

###

### Create a new department
POST http://localhost:8080/api/departments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Music",
  "description": "Study of sound and rhythm"
}

###

### Delete a department
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/departments/11
Accept: application/json

###

### ==================== COURSES ====================

### Get all courses
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Accept: application/json

###

### Get course by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Get courses filtered by department
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses?departmentId=1
Accept: application/json

###

### Get course that doesn't exist (should return 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/courses/999
Accept: application/json

###

### Create a new course
POST http://localhost:8080/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Machine Learning",
  "code": "CS401",
  "description": "Introduction to ML algorithms",
  "credits": 4,
  "departmentId": 1
}

###

### Delete a course
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/courses/11
Accept: application/json

###

### ==================== ENROLLMENTS ====================

### Get all enrollments
GET http://localhost:8080/api/enrollments
Accept: application/json

###

### Get enrollment by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/enrollments/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Get enrollments filtered by course
GET http://localhost:8080/api/enrollments?courseId=1
Accept: application/json

###

### Get enrollment that doesn't exist (should return 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/enrollments/999
Accept: application/json

###

### Create a new enrollment
POST http://localhost:8080/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentName": "John Doe",
  "studentEmail": "john.doe@university.edu",
  "courseId": 1
}

###

### Delete an enrollment
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/enrollments/11
Accept: application/json